abstract: >-
  Complete material for two linked sessions on artificial intelligence based
  clinical decision support systems, delivered at the Technology and Artificial
  Intelligence Literacy Training programme hosted by Akdeniz University in
  September 2026. The first session is a forty five minute lecture on what such
  systems are, why they fail in practice, and what makes them trustworthy. The
  second is a two hour workshop in which participants build a decision support
  prototype for their own clinical problem using generative artificial
  intelligence tools, with minimal direct coding. The repository contains the
  lecture source texts in Turkish and English, seven Jupyter notebooks, a prompt
  library given in both languages, governance templates, and Python modules that
  call the MIMIC-IV demo dataset over the web and implement an honest evaluation
  checklist.
keywords:
